**Given:**

Time (t) = 2 years

Increase in interest rate = 2%

Difference in interest accrued = ₹240

**Formula used:**

Simple Interest (SI) = dfrac{P times r times t}{100}

Difference in SI = dfrac{P times (r+2) times t}{100} - dfrac{P times r times t}{100}

**Calculation:**

240 = dfrac{P times 2 times 2}{100}

⇒ 240 = dfrac{4P}{100}

⇒ P = dfrac{240 times 100}{4}

⇒ P = 6000

**∴ The sum invested is ₹6000.**

